			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1783545343138,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "Definition: A node can have any number of children (up to N).\nConstraint: None. It is the most flexible and least optimized tree structure.\nKey Examples:\n  - Trie (Prefix Tree): Used for autocomplete and spell-checkers; nodes represent \n    characters in a string.\n  - B-Tree / B+ Tree: Used in database indexing where nodes hold large amounts of \n    data to minimize disk access.",
			"rawText": "Definition: A node can have any number of children (up to N).\nConstraint: None. It is the most flexible and least optimized tree structure.\nKey Examples:\n  - Trie (Prefix Tree): Used for autocomplete and spell-checkers; nodes represent \n    characters in a string.\n  - B-Tree / B+ Tree: Used in database indexing where nodes hold large amounts of \n    data to minimize disk access.",
			"fontSize": 20,
			"fontFamily": 8,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": "2cLxDqrz",
			"originalText": "Definition: A node can have any number of children (up to N).\nConstraint: None. It is the most flexible and least optimized tree structure.\nKey Examples:\n  - Trie (Prefix Tree): Used for autocomplete and spell-checkers; nodes represent \n    characters in a string.\n  - B-Tree / B+ Tree: Used in database indexing where nodes hold large amounts of \n    data to minimize disk access.",
			"autoResize": true,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"link": null
		},
